  "narrative": {
    "intro": "This ranking lists the largest federal contractors by contract obligations for FY2027 to date. Total obligations across the listed contractors equal $3.9B. TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP leads the list with $900M in obligations. FLUOR MARINE PROPULSION, LLC follows with $373M, and ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC ranks third with $167M. The list includes a mix of defense, logistics, professional services, and research entities, including AT&T ENTERPRISES, LLC at $166M and THUNDERCAT TECHNOLOGY, LLC at $154M. Stonex Financial Ltd and the California Institute of Technology appear with $144M and $128M respectively. Metropolitan Security Services, Inc. and FedEx Supply Chain Distribution System, Inc. each show $102M. Hanford Tank Waste Operations & Closure, LLC rounds out the top ten with $100M. These figures represent obligations recorded in the fiscal year to date and therefore reflect partial-year totals rather than a full fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top contractors by obligations in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP is the top contractor with $900M in obligations. FLUOR MARINE PROPULSION, LLC is second with $373M, and ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC is third with $167M. The top ten also include AT&T ENTERPRISES, LLC at $166M, THUNDERCAT TECHNOLOGY, LLC at $154M, and STONEX FINANCIAL LTD at $144M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What do these obligation figures represent?",
        "body": "The figures represent contract obligations recorded in FY2027 to date. The total obligations across the ranked contractors equal $3.9B. These are partial-year totals and do not represent a complete fiscal year."
      }
    ]
  },
